1
00:00:02,208 --> 00:00:03,000
Coffee went up again.

2
00:00:03,042 --> 00:00:04,000
Lend me ten bucks.

3
00:00:04,292 --> 00:00:06,000
One winning bet buys coffee for a month.

4
00:00:06,875 --> 00:00:08,083
You want a drink.

5
00:00:08,208 --> 00:00:10,125
Why are you predicting the universe?

6
00:00:11,375 --> 00:00:12,500
Because I know football.

7
00:00:13,917 --> 00:00:16,750
Then meet the people who make money from that sentence.

8
00:00:22,583 --> 00:00:24,792
Tiny stadium. Enormous cash register.

9
00:00:25,625 --> 00:00:27,083
Three different numbers.

10
00:00:27,167 --> 00:00:30,167
Money wagered. Revenue kept by the operator.

11
00:00:30,333 --> 00:00:31,833
Profit after costs.

12
00:00:32,042 --> 00:00:33,292
Never mix them up.

13
00:00:34,167 --> 00:00:35,875
Bet one hundred dollars ten times.

14
00:00:35,958 --> 00:00:37,208
That's a thousand wagered.

15
00:00:37,208 --> 00:00:38,542
My wallet is still tiny.

16
00:00:39,375 --> 00:00:42,875
Now, odds. Two possible results.

17
00:00:43,083 --> 00:00:44,958
Each pays one point nine.

18
00:00:44,958 --> 00:00:48,500
Bet a hundred, win, get one hundred ninety back.

19
00:00:48,583 --> 00:00:49,833
Including your stake.

20
00:00:50,833 --> 00:00:52,375
Where does the other ten go?

21
00:00:53,167 --> 00:00:56,292
A hundred on each side means two hundred collected.

22
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:58,292
Either winner gets one ninety.

23
00:00:58,292 --> 00:00:59,875
Ten stays in the till.

24
00:01:00,917 --> 00:01:02,875
The cash register scored before kickoff.

25
00:01:04,167 --> 00:01:05,875
In this balanced example.

26
00:01:06,125 --> 00:01:10,125
Real bookmakers face uneven bets, pricing errors and risk.

27
00:01:10,125 --> 00:01:12,083
They do not win on every match.

28
00:01:13,083 --> 00:01:16,708
One divided by one point nine is about fifty-two point six

29
00:01:16,708 --> 00:01:19,333
percent. Both sides add up above a hundred.

30
00:01:19,333 --> 00:01:21,500
That excess shows the markup.

31
00:01:24,792 --> 00:01:26,500
New door! Tiny stake.

32
00:01:26,625 --> 00:01:28,125
Giant prize. This one gets me.

33
00:01:28,917 --> 00:01:32,083
A parlay. Every selection must win.

34
00:01:32,250 --> 00:01:34,667
Three independent fifty-fifty outcomes?

35
00:01:34,917 --> 00:01:37,125
All three win only one time in eight.

36
00:01:38,125 --> 00:01:39,708
I only missed the last one!

37
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,208
The till loves the word only.

38
00:01:43,375 --> 00:01:45,708
Big payouts come with low probabilities.

39
00:01:45,708 --> 00:01:48,125
And discounts in the odds compound.

40
00:01:51,708 --> 00:01:53,750
Why are the horses circling a soup pot?

41
00:01:54,625 --> 00:01:57,333
Pool betting. Stakes go into one pot.

42
00:01:57,542 --> 00:01:59,333
The operator takes a stated deduction.

43
00:01:59,625 --> 00:02:01,458
Winning tickets divide what remains.

44
00:02:01,750 --> 00:02:03,500
Your final payout depends on the pool.

45
00:02:04,542 --> 00:02:05,542
Horses get a track.

46
00:02:05,667 --> 00:02:06,958
My money gets a drain.

47
00:02:10,667 --> 00:02:13,542
Free money! Finally, a universe with customer service.

48
00:02:14,417 --> 00:02:15,667
Read the conditions.

49
00:02:15,875 --> 00:02:18,292
Bonuses can require more wagering.

50
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:22,542
Notifications and live bets turn one match into dozens of decisions.

51
00:02:23,667 --> 00:02:25,292
So close! One more try.

52
00:02:25,375 --> 00:02:26,833
So close! Another try.

53
00:02:26,917 --> 00:02:27,542
So close!

54
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:31,042
Stop. Nearly winning is still losing.

55
00:02:31,250 --> 00:02:32,875
It can make you want another turn.

56
00:02:32,958 --> 00:02:35,292
It does not make the next win more likely.

57
00:02:38,750 --> 00:02:40,125
What about inside information?

58
00:02:40,208 --> 00:02:41,542
Are all the matches already scripted?

59
00:02:42,375 --> 00:02:44,417
Match fixing exists.

60
00:02:44,583 --> 00:02:46,417
An upset is not proof of it.

61
00:02:46,458 --> 00:02:50,083
Evidence has to identify what happened and who was involved.

62
00:02:51,125 --> 00:02:56,083
In twenty twenty-five, Turkey reported three hundred seventy-one referees with betting

63
00:02:56,083 --> 00:02:59,750
accounts. One hundred fifty-two had football betting records.

64
00:03:00,792 --> 00:03:02,958
Having an account, placing bets, fixing matches.

65
00:03:03,167 --> 00:03:04,000
Three different claims.

66
00:03:05,417 --> 00:03:09,833
Exactly. And that story about coach Bob Woolmer being murdered?

67
00:03:09,917 --> 00:03:13,917
Jamaican police later closed the case, accepting natural causes.

68
00:03:17,375 --> 00:03:19,250
This world looks suspiciously normal.

69
00:03:19,375 --> 00:03:20,917
Shops? Advertisements?

70
00:03:21,833 --> 00:03:24,375
Different places, different rules.

71
00:03:24,375 --> 00:03:26,208
Britain licenses operators.

72
00:03:26,208 --> 00:03:31,708
A twenty eighteen Supreme Court ruling let American states decide whether

73
00:03:31,708 --> 00:03:33,333
to authorize sports betting.

74
00:03:34,417 --> 00:03:35,292
I recognize those.

75
00:03:35,417 --> 00:03:36,792
FanDuel. DraftKings.

76
00:03:37,625 --> 00:03:41,833
Real operators. A legal business can still cost you money.

77
00:03:42,125 --> 00:03:44,583
And legal somewhere does not mean legal everywhere.

78
00:03:45,708 --> 00:03:49,042
Hong Kong authorizes Jockey Club businesses.

79
00:03:49,208 --> 00:03:51,375
Singapore has regulated operators.

80
00:03:51,708 --> 00:03:54,708
Mainland China has its own authorized lottery system.

81
00:03:55,708 --> 00:03:58,500
This foreign license is not an interdimensional passport.

82
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:04,042
Nor does a famous brand or a public-benefit purpose guarantee generous

83
00:04:04,042 --> 00:04:07,000
payouts. Read the actual allocation rules.

84
00:04:10,458 --> 00:04:11,375
One last door.

85
00:04:11,375 --> 00:04:12,208
No cash up front!

86
00:04:12,292 --> 00:04:13,958
They finally trust my football knowledge.

87
00:04:14,792 --> 00:04:16,833
They trust that you will owe them money.

88
00:04:17,917 --> 00:04:19,375
Why do the chips have teeth?

89
00:04:20,250 --> 00:04:25,000
Some illegal operations combine credit betting, debt and threats.

90
00:04:25,292 --> 00:04:28,167
No deposit can become a debt much bigger than your original

91
00:04:28,167 --> 00:04:28,750
budget.

92
00:04:29,792 --> 00:04:31,958
Owen Hanson is a real case.

93
00:04:32,083 --> 00:04:37,292
His criminal enterprise involved illegal gambling, drug trafficking and money laundering.

94
00:04:38,250 --> 00:04:42,958
In twenty seventeen, he received two hundred fifty-five months in prison.

95
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,875
More than twenty-one years.

96
00:04:45,958 --> 00:04:48,625
Being introduced by a friend is not a safety certificate.

97
00:04:50,083 --> 00:04:53,833
Right. An illegal book is not simply a cheaper app.

98
00:04:53,833 --> 00:04:57,708
And a licensed operator is not automatically a criminal enterprise.

99
00:04:57,958 --> 00:04:59,333
Keep the claims separate.

100
00:05:02,792 --> 00:05:05,625
After all those universes, did you find a guaranteed way to

101
00:05:05,625 --> 00:05:06,083
make money?

102
00:05:06,917 --> 00:05:07,667
Yes.

103
00:05:08,833 --> 00:05:09,500
Really?

104
00:05:10,625 --> 00:05:11,708
Sell coffee.

105
00:05:14,875 --> 00:05:16,333
What happened to my ten bucks?

106
00:05:17,250 --> 00:05:18,875
Still in your pocket.

107
00:05:20,458 --> 00:05:21,542
Biggest upset of the day.

108
00:05:21,625 --> 00:05:22,750
I did not place a bet.
